## Shortcuts that are false, and what the explicit structure of `A_∞` does give

Notation in (a)–(d): `F_0 := Polynomial.X ∈ 𝒫⁺`, so `T_{F_0} ∈ Λ` and `T_{F_0} ^{1/p} ∈ Λ`.

(a) **`A' ⧸ ϖA'` is (expected to be) a proper quotient of `A_∞ ⧸ ϖA_∞`.**  The element
   `z := T_{F_0} ^{1/p}/ϖ ∈ Λ[1/ϖ]` satisfies `z ^ p = T_{F_0}/ϖ ^ p ∈ A_∞` (`P(T_P)/ϖ ^ m ∈ A_∞`
   for `P = X`, `m = p`), hence `z ∈ pIntTower p A_∞ 1 ⊆ A'`; moreover `T_{F_0} ^{1/p}/ϖ ^ m ∈ A'`
   for *every* `m ≥ 1`, because its `p`-th power is `T_{F_0}/ϖ ^{mp} ∈ A_∞`.  So
   `T_{F_0} ^{1/p} ∈ ϖ ^ mA'` for every `m`.  Whether `T_{F_0} ^{1/p} ∈ ϖA_∞` (equivalently
   `T_{F_0} ^{1/p}/ϖ ∈ A_∞`) is a separate question — the `p`-th-power computation above does not
   answer it — but expected to fail: if it fails, the map `A_∞ ⧸ ϖA_∞ → A' ⧸ ϖA'` is *not*
   injective and the flatness of `A_∞ ⧸ ϖA_∞` over `A ⧸ (ϖ)` (`CSAlgPos_mod_varpi_flat`,
   sorry-free in this directory) does *not* transfer to `A'`.  In any case `A' ≠ A_∞` — the tower
   `pIntTower p A_∞ n` does not stabilise, as `T_{F_0} ^{1/p ^ n}/ϖ` needs level `n`.

(b) **`ϖ` is *not* a unit of `A'`.**  If `ϖ^{-1} ∈ A'` then `A' ⊇ Λ[ϖ^{-1}] = Λ[1/ϖ]` and
   `A' = Λ[1/ϖ]`; then `pA' = A'` and `B ⧸ pB ≅ A' ⧸ pA' = 0`, contradicting the truth of the
   requested statement (ČS `Andre-lem` gives `B ⧸ pB` faithfully flat over the nontrivial ring
   `A ⧸ (p)`).  So the target is not vacuous and no "`A' = Λ[1/ϖ]`" shortcut exists.

(c) **Correction (session of 2026-10-13, second sitting).**  The earlier version of this file
   recorded as *false* the one-step statement "`R' ⧸ ϖ` is flat over `R ⧸ ϖ` for every subring
   `R ⊆ Λ[1/ϖ]`" with the alleged counterexample `R = k[x ^ 2] ⊆ k[x][1/x]`, `ϖ = x ^ 2`.  That
   example is **wrong**: `k[x^2]` is the polynomial ring `k[Z]` in the variable `Z = x ^ 2`, so
   `R ⧸ ϖR = k[Z]/(Z) ≅ k` is a *field*, over which every module is flat.  The one-step statement
   is nevertheless false in general, but the valid counterexample is different: over
   `R = k[u ^ p, v ^ p, uv] ⊆ S = k[u,v]` one has `u, v ∈ Z := {z : z ^ p ∈ R}` and hence
   `R ⊔ closure Z = k[u,v]`, which is *not* `R`-flat (the relation `uv ∈ R` is the obstruction).
   With a *regular sequence* criterion the flatness of one step does hold; the point is that no
   purely formal argument settles the question and the specific structure of `Λ[1/ϖ]` is needed.

(d) **Positive structural facts that *are* available (useful for the tower analysis).**
   * `Λ ⧸ ϖ ^ N` is a quotient of `(A ⧸ ϖ ^ N)[X_{(F,n)} : F ∈ 𝒫⁺, n ≥ 0]` modulo the relations
     `X_{(F,n+1)} ^ p = X_{(F,n)}`; for `N ≤ p` (in particular `N = 1` and `N = p`, where
     `A ⧸ ϖ ^ p ≅ A ⧸ p` is perfect by `isFrobIsoMod`) every element of `Λ ⧸ ϖ ^ N` is a `p`-th
     power: `a = b ^ p` and `X_n ^ e = (X_{n+1} ^ e) ^ p`.  Hence `Λ ⧸ ϖ ^ N` is *perfect* for
     `N ∈ {1, p}`.
   * Since `I_∞` is `ϖ`-divisible, `A_∞ ⧸ ϖ ^ N A_∞ = (A_∞ ⧸ I_∞) ⧸ (ϖ ^ N)
     ≅ (Λ ⧸ (P(T_P))) ⧸ (ϖ ^ N)` (using the proved `Work.DSM2p.quotJ_equiv_R`, i.e.
     `A_∞ ⧸ I_∞ ≅ Λ ⧸ CSIdeal`), so `A_∞ ⧸ ϖ ^ N` is a *quotient* of the perfect ring
     `Λ ⧸ ϖ ^ N`: it is perfect too for `N ∈ {1, p}`, which is exactly the ČS remark that
     "every element of `A_∞ ⧸ (ϖ ^ p)` is a `p`-th power".
   * Consequently (with `sum_pow_sub_mem`, i.e. additivity of Frobenius mod `ϖ ^ p`, and
     `p`-integral closedness of `A'`): if `z ∈ Λ[1/ϖ]` has `z ^ p ∈ A_∞`, then there is
     `a ∈ A_∞` with `z - a ∈ ϖA'`.  This is the level-`0` case of the mod-`ϖ` surjectivity
     `A' ⊆ A_∞ + ϖA'`; the higher tower levels would need the intermediate rings `pIntTower p A_∞ n`
     to have Frobenius surjective modulo `ϖ ^ p`, which is *not* automatic.
-/


namespace Work.DSM2p

universe u

/-- `A_∞ = CSAlgPos A p ϖ`, the subring `A[T_F^{1/p^n}][F(T_F)/ϖ^m] ⊆ Λ[1/ϖ]` of the
Česnavičius–Scholze construction, is an `A`-algebra via the canonical map `A → Λ → Λ[1/ϖ]`. -/
noncomputable instance CSAlgPos.instAlgebra (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (p : ℕ) (ϖ : A) :
    Algebra A ↥(CSAlgPos A p ϖ) :=
  (RingHom.codRestrict (AAlgHomLocPos A p ϖ) _ (AAlgHomLocPos_mem_CSAlgPos A p ϖ)).toAlgebra

/-- The `A ⧸ (ϖ)`-module structure on `A_∞ ⧸ ϖA_∞`.  As in `ConstructionPos` for `B`, instance
search does not find it for the concrete abbreviation, so it is recorded explicitly. -/
noncomputable instance CSAlgPos.instModuleQuot (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (p : ℕ) (ϖ : A) :
    Module (A ⧸ Ideal.span {ϖ})
      (↥(CSAlgPos A p ϖ) ⧸ (Ideal.span {ϖ}).map (algebraMap A ↥(CSAlgPos A p ϖ))) :=
  (inferInstance : Algebra _ _).toModule

/-- **The ideal `I_∞ ⊆ A_∞`.**  It is generated by the elements `F(T_F) / ϖ ^ m`
(`F ∈ 𝒫⁺`, `m : ℕ`) that define the Česnavičius–Scholze ring `A_∞` as a subring of `Λ[1/ϖ]`.
This is the ideal of the construction (`Design §2`, `I_∞`), the input of the ``A_∞/I_∞ is flat''
step (`CSAlgPos_quot_CSIdealPos_flat`). -/
noncomputable def CSIdealPos (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (p : ℕ) (ϖ : A) :
    Ideal ↥(CSAlgPos A p ϖ) :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range (fun q : MonicPolysPos A × ℕ =>
    (⟨(algebraMap (RootAlgPos A p) (RootAlgLocPos A p ϖ)
          (Polynomial.aeval (rootVarPos A p q.1) q.1.1) *
        IsLocalization.Away.invSelf (algebraMap A (RootAlgPos A p) ϖ) ^ q.2),
      Subring.subset_closure (Set.mem_union_right _ ⟨q, rfl⟩)⟩ : ↥(CSAlgPos A p ϖ))))

/-- The `A`-algebra structure on `A_∞ ⧸ I_∞` (recorded explicitly, as instance search does not
find it for the concrete abbreviation). -/
noncomputable instance CSIdealPos.instAlgebra (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (p : ℕ) (ϖ : A) :
    Algebra A (↥(CSAlgPos A p ϖ) ⧸ CSIdealPos A p ϖ) :=
  RingHom.toAlgebra ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (CSIdealPos A p ϖ)).comp
    (algebraMap A ↥(CSAlgPos A p ϖ)))

/-- The `A ⧸ (p)`-module structure on `A' ⧸ pA'` (`A' = CSIntegralClosurePos`), recorded
explicitly for the same reason as in `ConstructionPos`. -/
noncomputable instance CSIntegralClosurePos.instModuleQuotP (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (p : ℕ)
    (ϖ : A) :
    Module (A ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : A)})
      (↥(CSIntegralClosurePos A p ϖ) ⧸
        (Ideal.span {(p : A)}).map (algebraMap A ↥(CSIntegralClosurePos A p ϖ))) :=
  (inferInstance : Algebra _ _).toModule

/-- The `A ⧸ (ϖ)`-module structure on `A' ⧸ ϖA'` (`A' = CSIntegralClosurePos`). -/
noncomputable instance CSIntegralClosurePos.instModuleQuotVarpi (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
    (p : ℕ) (ϖ : A) :
    Module (A ⧸ Ideal.span {ϖ})
      (↥(CSIntegralClosurePos A p ϖ) ⧸
        (Ideal.span {ϖ}).map (algebraMap A ↥(CSIntegralClosurePos A p ϖ))) :=
  (inferInstance : Algebra _ _).toModule

/-- **The `p`-adic completion does not change the reduction modulo `p`.**
For every commutative ring `E`, the level-one reduction
`Ê ⧸ pÊ → E ⧸ pE` of the `p`-adic completion `Ê = AdicCompletion (p) E` is a ring isomorphism
(`AdicCompletion.ker_evalOneₐ_eq_map` identifies the kernel of `evalOneₐ` with `pÊ`). -/
noncomputable def adicCompletion_quot_span_p_ringEquiv (E : Type u) [CommRing E] (p : ℕ) :
    (AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : E)}) E ⧸
        Ideal.span {(p : AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : E)}) E)}) ≃+*
      (E ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : E)}) := by
  haveI hfg : (Ideal.span {(p : E)}).FG := ⟨{(p : E)}, by simp⟩
  have hker := AdicCompletion.ker_evalOneₐ_eq_map (Ideal.span {(p : E)}) hfg
  have hspan : (Ideal.span {(p : E)}).map (algebraMap E (AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : E)}) E))
      = Ideal.span {(p : AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : E)}) E)} := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_natCast]
  exact (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq ((hker.trans hspan).symm)).trans
    (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective
      (f := (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ (Ideal.span {(p : E)})).toRingHom)
      (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ_surjective _))

/-- **The `p`-adic completion does not change the reduction modulo `p`, as an algebra
isomorphism.**  For every commutative ring `A`, every `A`-algebra `E` and every `p : ℕ`,
`Ê ⧸ pÊ ≅ E ⧸ pE` as `A ⧸ (p)`-algebras.  (Proved in
`Submission/Work/DSM2p/CSCompletionPos_quot_p_algEquiv.lean` by a colleague; reproduced here,
with the same proof, so that this file is self-contained.) -/
noncomputable def adicCompletion_quot_span_p_algEquiv (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (p : ℕ)
    (E : Type u) [CommRing E] [Algebra A E] :
    (AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : E)}) E ⧸
        (Ideal.span {(p : A)}).map (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (Ideal.span {(p : E)}) E))) ≃ₐ[A ⧸ Ideal.span {(p : A)}]
      (E ⧸ (Ideal.span {(p : A)}).map (algebraMap A E)) := by
  set J : Ideal E := Ideal.span {(p : E)} with hJdef
  set I_E : Ideal E := (Ideal.span {(p : A)}).map (algebraMap A E) with hIEdef
  have hJE : J = I_E := by
    rw [hJdef, hIEdef, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_natCast]
  have hFG : J.FG := by rw [hJdef]; exact Submodule.fg_span_singleton (p : E)
  have hJK : Ideal.map (algebraMap E (AdicCompletion J E)) J =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap E (AdicCompletion J E)) I_E := by rw [hJE]
  have hIker : (Ideal.span {(p : A)}).map (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion J E)) =
      RingHom.ker (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J).toRingHom := by
    rw [AdicCompletion.ker_evalOneₐ_eq_map J hFG, hJK, hIEdef, Ideal.map_map,
      ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A E (AdicCompletion J E)]
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J).toRingHom :=
    fun x => AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ_surjective J x
  let e : (AdicCompletion J E ⧸ (Ideal.span {(p : A)}).map (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion J E))) ≃+*
      (E ⧸ I_E) :=
    (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq hIker).trans
      ((RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective hsurj).trans (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq hJE))
  refine AlgEquiv.ofRingEquiv (f := e) ?_
  intro x
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  rw [Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_quotient_map_quotient,
    Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_quotient_map_quotient]
  simp only [e, RingEquiv.trans_apply, Ideal.quotEquivOfEq_mk,
    RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective_apply_mk]
  rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply A E (AdicCompletion J E)]
  have hstep : (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J).toRingHom
      ((algebraMap E (AdicCompletion J E)) ((algebraMap A E) a)) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk J ((algebraMap A E) a) := by
    change (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J) ((algebraMap E (AdicCompletion J E)) ((algebraMap A E) a)) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk J ((algebraMap A E) a)
    rw [AlgHom.commutes (AdicCompletion.evalOneₐ J), Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]
  rw [hstep, Ideal.quotEquivOfEq_mk]

/-- **The target reduces to `A' ⧸ pA'`.**  For every `P : PerfectoidData p A`, the faithful
flatness of `B ⧸ pB` over `A ⧸ (p)` (the requested lemma) follows from the faithful flatness of
`A' ⧸ pA'` over `A ⧸ (p)`, because the two are isomorphic as `A ⧸ (p)`-algebras
(`adicCompletion_quot_span_p_algEquiv`); faithful flatness transfers along an algebra
equivalence.  This isolates the *(H2)* input of `DESIGN.md` as a statement about the `p`-integral
closure `A' = CSIntegralClosurePos A p ϖ` alone. -/
